   "source": [
    "# Fine-tune capstrack-duplication v4 (Colab)\n",
    "\n",
    "Retrains the duplication judge on `dataset-v3.jsonl`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What the last retrain got wrong**\n",
    "\n",
    "v2's training data carried 30 mid-range examples against 103 at the extremes,\n",
    "and all 30 of the middle sat on three subjects - door locks, Odoo, and\n",
    "registrar scheduling. Seventeen were door locks. So the model did not learn\n",
    "\"partial overlap scores in the middle\"; it learned \"door locks score 63\", and\n",
    "on a crop-disease pair it had never seen it answered 85 where a human said 52.\n",
    "\n",
    "It was also trained against the old judge prompt, which ended with \"the score\n",
    "must be low regardless of how many words they share\" - so it learned to answer\n",
    "a question the app no longer asks.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What `dataset-v3.jsonl` changes**\n",
    "\n",
    "- 76 mid-range examples against 91 at the extremes, spread over 71 topic\n",
    "  pairings with no pairing holding more than five of the middle\n",
    "- the 30-39 band is populated; v2 had nothing there at all\n",
    "- every prompt built against the current judge prompt\n",
    "- no reason opens \"Different domain\" (v2: 23 of 56 low examples), and none\n",
    "  rests on both studies replacing a manual process - true of 111 of the 196\n",
    "  studies in the archive, so it distinguishes nothing\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stop at cell 9.** It scores 15 held-out pairs and tells you whether this\n",
    "model beats the one already installed. If it does not, exporting is 25 minutes\n",
    "spent on a model you would not install.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cells in order. Set **Runtime -> Change runtime type -> T4 GPU** first.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
